   ∫_0^1 φ(e/e(0)) <= D.
9. Finally 4e(0) <= 1 and φ(sx) <= sφ(x) give p = φ(4e) <= φ(e/e(0)), so d <= D. Also e(0) > 0, since otherwise e ≡ 0
   and p ≡ 0.
10. P58 gives d >= 1/C, which contradicts C < 1/D. ∎
